    "body": "**Account 404: Hearthwick Train (The Brack Convoy)**\n\n*Status:* OPEN\n*Cargo Logged:* None this season.\n*Tolls Paid:* None this season.\n\n*Note for the junior clerks:*\nDo not strike Account 404 from the ledger. Yes, they are thirty years late. Yes, the Reed road is closed. But Compact Law states clearly that a train is \"On the Road\" until the tally-stick is surrendered at the desk and the wheel-tax is settled. We do not presume the fate of a convoy. We are accountants, not priests. Carry the balance forward to the Thaw-wick quarter.\n\n*(Beneath the fold, in a newer and smaller hand:)*\n\n**Thaw-wick quarter:**\nBalance carried forward, as instructed. Another wick of no cargo and no tolls. The other under-clerks have taken to calling this the ghost account, and they waste good ink complaining of it. Waste is not the Compact's way either. A train is on the road until the tally-stick is surrendered. My task is only to keep the desk ready for it. — Pell, under-clerk"
